title: The Terraform behind this week
subtitle: week-21-bluegreen-ecs - what each file does, and how big it actually is
width: 1050
---
week-21-bluegreen-ecs/
│
├── terraform/
│   ├── environments/dev/          # what this environment is
│   │   ├── main.tf          79    # HCP backend, provider pin, default VPC lookup,
│   │   │                          # and the single call into the module
│   │   ├── variables.tf     21    # app_version, serve_root, bake_time_in_minutes
│   │   └── outputs.tf        8    # the ALB URL you curl
│   │
│   └── modules/service/           # HOW it is built -- all 16 resources live here
│       ├── main.tf         347    # ALB + listener + rule, two target groups,
│       │                          # ECS cluster/task/service, alarm, logs, IAM
│       ├── variables.tf     74    # every knob, with a default
│       └── outputs.tf        6
│
└── scripts/
    ├── watch_shift.sh       76    # polls the ALB during a deployment and counts
    │                              # responses by version -- the client's view
    └── cleanup.sh           44    # teardown verification, run after the destroy


# WHY IT IS SPLIT THIS WAY
#
# environments/dev answers "what am I deploying, and where does the state live".
# modules/service answers "how is it built". Changing the version deployed is a
# variable change in environments/dev; changing the ARCHITECTURE is a change in
# modules/service. A reader replicating this only needs to read one of them.
#
# 347 lines is most of the week. The block that makes it blue/green rather than
# a rolling update is nine of them.
